🚗 Driver Drowsiness Detection Project

📁 Step 01: Open Project Folder

Open the main project directory in your preferred IDE (e.g., VS Code, PyCharm).

🧪 Step 02: OpenCV Practice (Haar Cascade Method)
File: haar_cascade_method.py

This is a practice implementation using OpenCV’s Haar Cascade classifiers.

⚠️ Note:
        This method is simple and less accurate
        It is not recommended for the final project
        Pre-trained Models:
                          haar_face.xml → Used for face detection
                          haar_eye.xml → Used for eye detection

These models are directly downloaded from the OpenCV GitHub repository.

▶️ How to Test:

Run the file to check basic OpenCV face and eye detection:

python haar_cascade_method.py


🧠 Step 03: Main Project (EAR Method)

File: EAR_method.py

This is the main and recommended implementation of the project.

It uses the Eye Aspect Ratio (EAR) technique to detect drowsiness more accurately.

Pre-trained Model:     
                  shape_predictor_68_face_landmark.dat

📌 This model is used to:
                        Detect facial landmarks
                        Extract eye landmarks
                        Calculate EAR (Eye Aspect Ratio)
                        Detect drowsiness based on eye closure


🔔 Alarm System
alarm.wav → Audio file used for alerting when drowsiness is detected

When the system detects prolonged eye closure, it will trigger this alarm sound.
